#subtitle: Working hours, safety regulations, and unemployment insurance.

= Labor Rights

Under the direction of Francisco Largo Caballero and the UGT, the Ministry of Labor has become the vanguard of the Social Republic. Through executive decrees and various reform, we can transform the balance of power between capital and labor.

@labor_rights_menu

- @termino_municipal: Enact the *Ley de Término Municpal*.
- @laboreo_forzoso: Enact the *Decreto de Laboreo Forzoso*.
- @working_hours: Enforce the 8-hour workday in industry and agriculture.
- @shorten_hours: Shorten work hours less than 8-hour workdays.
- @safety: Develop and enforce safety regulations.
- @social_insurance: Fund the Maternity Insurance & Workers' Pensions.
- @root: Do not enact any policies.
- @cancel_advisor_action

@termino_municipal
view-if: termino != 1
on-arrival: termino = 1; rural_psoe += 8; cnt_militancy -= 1 if Q.cnt_militancy > 0; capital_strike_progress += 1; prr_relation -=5; unemployed -= 0.3;

We sign the *Ley de Término Municipal*, barring landowners from importing cheap, unorganized migrant labor from other municipalities to undercut local wage rates.

However, in large municipalities, this has resulted in jornaleros who used to work in nearby fields in other municipalities having to travel long distances within their own municipality to get to work.


@laboreo_forzoso
view-if: laboreo != 1
on-arrival: laboreo = 1; rural_psoe += 8; cnt_militancy -= 1 if Q.cnt_militancy > 0; land_reform_progress += 0.5; capital_strike_progress += 2; prr_relation -=5; unemployed -= 0.3; coup_progress += 1; smallholders_ap += 7; coalition_dissent += 1 if in_republican_socialist_conjunction;

In response to reactionary landowners who refuse to plant their fields as a passive protest against our government, hoping to induce artificial famine and social chaos, we institute mandatory cultivation rules. Fields left intentionally idle will be temporarily seized and worked directly by municipal peasant committees.

Thousands of unemployed laborers are immediately put back to work in the fields. However, conservative parties and right-wing newspapers accuse us of enacting hidden Bolshevism and violating fundamental property rights.

@working_hours
view-if: working_hours < 2
on-arrival: working_hours += 1; besteiristas_dissent -= 8; caballeristas_dissent -= 5; besteiristas_strength += 5; rural_psoe += 7*(1-dissent); workers_psoe += 3*(1-dissent); prr_relation -= 4; coalition_dissent += 1 if in_republican_socialist_conjunction; capital_strike_progress += 1 if prr_relation <= 30; labor_goal_completed = 1; inflation += 0.1; economic_growth -= 0.1; unemployed -= 0.2;

While the 8-hour day existed on paper in Spanish cities, rural landlords routinely forced laborers to work 12 to 14 hours during harvest season for starvation pay. We deploy dedicated Ministry inspectors to enforce maximum hours strictly in both field and factory.

Farmers are forced to hire extra hands to complete seasonal harvests, providing immediate employment relief. Employers argue that agricultural work cannot be regulated like a factory clock and that production costs will skyrocket.

@shorten_hours
view-if: working_hours >= 2 and unemployed >= 15
subtitle: Could we induce more hiring and reduce unemployment by reducing work hours?
on-arrival: working_hours += 1; labor_dissent -= 8; left_dissent -= 5; labor_strength += 5; rural_psoe += 7*(1-dissent); workers_psoe += 4*(1-dissent); prr_relation -= 8; dlr_relation -= 8; coalition_dissent += 1; capital_strike_progress += 1; labor_goal_completed = 1; unemployed -= 0.4; economic_growth -= 0.2;

Some in the labor movement argue that by reducing the maximum number of hours worked, employers would be induced to hire more workers, reducing unemployment. Employers, however, resist this policy, arguing for more flexibility in hiring and firing.


@safety
on-arrival: workers_safety += 1; labor_dissent -= 5; labor_strength += 2; workers_psoe += 5*(1-dissent); capital_strike_progress += 1 if workers_safety >= 3

The Labor Ministry works on developing and enforcing safety regulations, in order to ensure healty working conditions for the proletariat. [? if workers_safety >= 3 : Businesses have begun to argue that our focus on safety is overbearing and unnecessary, interfering with the economy. ?]

@social_insurance
choose-if: budget >= 1
unavailable-subtitle: We need at least 1 budget.
on-arrival: budget -= 1; welfare += 1; workers_psoe += 4*(1-dissent); rural_psoe += 3*(1-dissent); middle_psoe += 2*(1-dissent); unemployed_psoe += 5*(1-dissent)

We allocate state funds to launch the compulsory Maternity Insurance (*Seguro de Maternidad*)—providing paid leave, medical care, and nursing stipends for working mothers—and increase state contributions to the old-age pension fund (*Retiro Obrero*).
